{:edb/db-before-t 1664 :edb/db-after-t 1665 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534977 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:53:42.424Z" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110374 1071 "![](images/8b/8bc5a70179a245c26f766e7c0efb36b508d259746a6a92b02c4d423d39940d5a.png)\n\n  \n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AC=BD$\n\nII. $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$\n\nIII. $\\overline{AB}$ is congruent to $\\overline{BD}$" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110374 1071 "![](images/8b/8bc5a70179a245c26f766e7c0efb36b508d259746a6a92b02c4d423d39940d5a.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AC=BD$\n2. $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$\n3. $\\overline{AB}$ is congruent to $\\overline{BD}$" 13194139534977 17592186045417 false] [17592186110374 1074 "Let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that $AC= BD=5$ units.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $AB=CD=3$ units, we have that $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$.\n\n- Statement III is false since $AB=3$, while $BD = 5.$ So, $\\overline{AB}\\ncong \\overline{BD}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110374 1074 "Let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that $AC= BD=5$ units.\n- Statement II is true. Since $AB=CD=3$ units, we have that $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$.\n- Statement III is false since $AB=3$, while $BD = 5$. So, $\\overline{AB}\\ncong \\overline{BD}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534977 17592186045417 false] [17592186110375 1074 "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}.$" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110375 1074 "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}$." 13194139534977 17592186045417 false] [17592186110376 1071 "For the diagram shown below, which of the following statements are true?\n\n![](images/79/793dacde520b1be4aa4a1e023760a06d1db5fe23266ec1277efe948e8ca04ab1.png)\n\n1. The segments $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ are congruent\n2. $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BE}$\n3. $BE = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$" 13194139534977 17592186045417 false] [17592186110376 1071 "For the diagram shown below, which of the following statements are true? \n\n![](images/79/793dacde520b1be4aa4a1e023760a06d1db5fe23266ec1277efe948e8ca04ab1.png)\n\n \n\nI. The segments $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BE}$\n\nIII. $BE = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110376 1074 "Let's look at the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. In the picture, both $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BD}$.\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, we can see that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ have different hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BC} \\not\\cong \\overline{BE}$.\n- Statement III is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have different hash marks, so\n$\\overline{BE} \\not\\cong \\overline{BD}$.\nHence, ${BE} \\neq {BD}$, and since ${BD} = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$, we have $BE \\neq 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139534977 17592186045417 false] [17592186110376 1074 "Let's look at the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. In the picture, both $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have the same double hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, we can see that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BC} \\not\\cong \\overline{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BE} \\not\\cong \\overline{BD}.\n$$\n\nHence, ${BE} \\neq {BD},$ and since ${BD} = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$, we have $BE \\neq 4\\,\\textrm{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110741 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446549 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110741 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446552 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110742 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446545 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110742 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446553 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446546 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446547 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446548 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446550 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446551 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186110834 1050 420.0 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186111834 1064 "When two line segments have the same length, they are **congruent** segments. To indicate that the line segments $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{CD}$ are congruent we write\n$\\overline{AB} \\:\\:{\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\cong}}\\:\\: \\overline{CD}$,\nand we use special marks like in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d7fd26fce7dce67fa57769db3e96be503051be5c7d2c7714ed48927547d5165.png)\n\nWe can also write\n\n$$\nAB \\:{\\color{blue}=}\\: CD\n$$\n\nwhich means that the measure of $\\overline{AB}$ is equal to the measure of $\\overline{CD}$.\n\n**Watch out!** The equation\n\n$$\n\\overline{AB} = \\overline{CD}\n$$\n\nis only true when both $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{CD}$ correspond to the same exact segment. When the segments are distinct, we should use the symbol $\\cong$ to represent that the two segments are separate but that they have the same length." 13194139534977 17592186045417 false] [17592186111834 1064 "When two line segments have the same length, they are **congruent** segments. To indicate that the line segments $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{CD}$ are congruent we write \n\n$$\n\\overline{AB} \\:\\:{\\color{red}\\boldsymbol{\\cong}}\\:\\: \\overline{CD},\n$$\n\nand we use special marks like in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d7fd26fce7dce67fa57769db3e96be503051be5c7d2c7714ed48927547d5165.png)\n\nWe can also write \n\n$$\nAB \\:{\\color{blue}=}\\: CD,\n$$\n\nwhich means that the measure of $\\overline{AB}$ is equal to the measure of $\\overline{CD}.$\n\n**Watch out!** The equation \n\n$$\n\\overline{AB} = \\overline{CD}\n$$\n\nis only true when both $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{CD}$ correspond to the same exact segment. When the segments are distinct, we should use the symbol $\\cong$ to represent that the two segments are separate but that they have the same length." 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446491 1080 "I only" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446491 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446491 1083 #uuid "020499ba-78b6-5552-952e-1513094a7f43" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446492 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446492 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446492 1083 #uuid "0538352e-c960-5edd-b769-4afa4dadefe2" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446493 1080 "II and III only" 13194139534977 17592186045417 true] [17592186446493 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534977 175921860